    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup today hinges on exploiting favorable matchups against Zac Gallen, who serves as the catalyst for our highest-scoring cluster. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (71.78) headlines the squad, benefiting not just from his elite contact profile, but from a \"slow delivery\" factor against Valdez that elevates his stolen base potential\u2014a critical consideration given our strategy to emphasize speed. Similarly, the trio of **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65), **Luis Arraez** (64.18), and **Matt Chapman** (62.67) all receive significant boosts from the Gallen matchup. **Jung Hoo Lee** in particular is primed for a massive outing, with his leadoff spot and platoon advantage combining for a 10% boost, making him our most efficient high-ceiling play.\n\nWhile we are deep today, the bench was a tight squeeze. **Jeremiah Jackson** (39.75) was the most difficult exclusion, falling just shy of the 40.0 efficiency floor required to warrant a start. While he offers some value against the slow delivery of McClanahan, his projected spot in the seventh slot dragged his overall score down, leaving him as the primary pivot should any late lineup changes occur. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Gavin Sheets** (43.64); despite the platoon edge, he faces a daunting task against Yamamoto, whose elite skill profile (3.33 xERA) necessitates a conservative outlook. **Will Smith** (58.02) and **Daulton Varsho** (48.46) remain functional, but they carry the risk of slightly suppressed output due to park factors and platoon disadvantages, respectively. With **Cal Raleigh** still sidelined on the IL, our defensive and offensive coverage remains focused on high-contact veterans and the remaining speed threats in the middle infield.",
